{"author":{"login":"Copilot"},"body":"`hostile_fleets` here counts every fleet currently in the sector whose owner is in a hostile/war relationship with the player, independent of `fog`. The resulting threat meter (and the \"Hostile contacts detected (N)\" strategic note) are then rendered for any sector the player has at least Explored — and the count itself reflects fleets the player has no current visibility on. For a sector in `FogState::Explored` (or even `Visible` with hidden enemy fleets), this leaks intel that the rest of this screen takes care to hide (e.g. owner/visibility gating just above). Consider restricting the hostile-fleet count to fleets the player can actually observe (e.g. using `visible_star_ids`/`star_fog_state`) or suppressing the threat meter / hostile note when the sector is not `Visible`.","id":3320909115,"line":454,"path":"crates/game_tui/src/screens/sector_overview.rs"}
{"author":{"login":"Copilot"},"body":"`hostile_here` is computed from all `game_state.fleets` at the selected star regardless of fog state, then fed into the threat meter that is rendered even when `fog` is `Unexplored`/`Explored`. The fog-aware code immediately above hides owner/colony/fleet counts for unexplored systems, but the threat meter still encodes the true hostile presence (e.g. a non-zero bar at an unexplored star reveals that an unseen hostile fleet sits there). Consider gating `hostile_here` (and the meter) on what the player can actually see — e.g. only count fleets at stars in `visible_stars`, or skip the meter when `fog` is not `Visible`.","id":3320909124,"line":678,"path":"crates/game_tui/src/screens/sector_map.rs"}
{"author":{"login":"Copilot"},"body":"`page_block` already wraps its title argument as ` {title} ` (see `components/chrome.rs`). Passing `format!(\" {} — Systems \", sector_name)` here results in a doubly-padded title like `\"  Andoria — Systems  \"` in the rendered border. Pass the raw `format!(\"{sector_name} — Systems\")` (without the surrounding spaces) and let `page_block` do the padding, for consistency with the other call sites that pass a bare title.","id":3320909144,"line":108,"path":"crates/game_tui/src/screens/sector_map.rs"}

